{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Likelihood.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Likelihood.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"likelihood likelihood","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Likelihood.md","fileName":"Likelihood.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Likelihood","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 21:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Probability Foundations]] · [[Count Models and Empirical Bayes]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Probability Foundations","Count Models and Empirical Bayes","Maximum Likelihood Estimation","bayesianprogramming.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Likelihood.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Likelihood.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"likelihood likelihood","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Likelihood.md","fileName":"Likelihood.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Likelihood","heading":"Likelihood","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Likelihood evaluates how compatible observed data is with a proposed hypothesis or parameter value. Written as $P(data \\mid hypothesis)$, it is viewed as a function of the hypothesis while the observed data remains fixed.\n\nLikelihood weights prior alternatives during Bayesian inference and supplies the objective for maximum-likelihood estimation. It is not generally normalized across hypothesis values until combined with the other model factors.\n\nFor independent observations, the source multiplies their model probabilities to form a joint likelihood. Holding the observed counts fixed while varying a Poisson rate turns this expression into the function optimized by [[Maximum Likelihood Estimation]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Probability Foundations","Count Models and Empirical Bayes","Maximum Likelihood Estimation","bayesianprogramming.